{
  "tema": 7152,
  "slug": "fracciones",
  "titulo": "Expressing fractions",
  "subtitulo": "Un tercio, dos quintos, la mitad, el doble.",
  "foto": "t07.jpg",
  "regla": "Fractions: cardinal + ordinal number like English (un cuarto, dos quintos); 1/2 = la mitad, 1/3 = un tercio; double = el doble. Plural when the top number is more than one.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Don't mix up **fractions** (a part of a whole: _half, a third, a quarter_) and **ordinal numbers** (an order: _1st, 2nd, 3rd_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Fractions work like English: a **cardinal** number on top and an **ordinal** below: **un quinto** (_one fifth_), **dos quintos** (_two fifths_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Fraction",
            "Spanish"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "1/2",
              "un medio / la mitad"
            ],
            [
              "1/3",
              "un tercio"
            ],
            [
              "1/4",
              "un cuarto"
            ],
            [
              "1/5",
              "un quinto"
            ],
            [
              "2/3",
              "dos tercios"
            ],
            [
              "3/4",
              "tres cuartos"
            ],
            [
              "1/10",
              "un décimo"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Like in English, the bottom number is **plural** when the top number is more than one: **dos tercios**, **tres cuartos**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Third** in a fraction is **tercio**, not **tercero**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "For _half_ and _double_ use the article: **la mitad** (_half_), **el doble** (_double_). **La mitad de la pizza**, **el doble de dinero**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **la mitad** for half, **el doble** for twice. The rest, count them like English."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Me comí ==dos tercios== de la pizza.",
              "en": "I ate two thirds of the pizza."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Un cuarto== de la población votó en contra.",
              "en": "A quarter of the population voted against."
            },
            {
              "es": "Solo puse ==la mitad== de la harina.",
              "en": "I only put in half the flour."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ahora gano ==el doble== que antes.",
              "en": "Now I earn double what I used to."
            },
            {
              "es": "Faltan ==tres cuartos== de hora para la marea alta.",
              "en": "There are three quarters of an hour until high tide."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Un quinto== del huerto es para hierbas.",
              "en": "A fifth of the garden is for herbs."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
